  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-fmt-2b/ix-delete-reinsert-ladder: no public read between steps (only the whole-file hash existed for the middle steps). Delete then reinsert of one index key: key 100 is deleted, then inserted again. Asks how the entry is retired and re-added and whether the statistic follows; count, minimum, maximum and the index statistics are read back after each step. IxM: 602 Long primary-key entries (1..301 and 303..603), no other column. Images: 'before' (the fixture copy as given), then one kept image of the closed file after each step; every step opens the database read/write, makes its mutation and closes it, with the DBEngine still alive.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
